Same reads as follows;
The heads under which compensation is awarded in personal injury cases are the SCCH-10 following;
Pecuniary damages (special damages)
(i) Expenses relating to treatment, hospitalization, Medicines, transportation, nourishing food and miscellaneous expenditure.

Loss of earnings (and other gains) which the injured would have made had he not been injured, comprising):
 Loss of earning during the period of  treatment;
b. Loss of future earning on account of permanent disability.
